experiment_sc1 {'measures_claim_target': True, 'sound': True, 'via': 'llm', 'status': 'judged', 'answered_by': {'attempt': 1, 'model': 'openai/gpt-6.1-sol'}, 'reason': 'The completed result is statistically plausible and internally consistent. Requested-file accuracy is 1,175/1,200 = 97.9167%; the confusion-matrix diagonal sums to 1,175, with 300 examples per class. The permitted/forbidden counts sum to 589 + 586 = 1,175, and authorization-correct/incorrect subgroup counts sum to 1,052 + 123 = 1,175 across 1,075 + 125 = 1,200 problems. The reported Wilson interval and exact binomial tail probability are consistent with these counts. Development-selected validation accuracy of 1,007/1,024 is plausibly close to test accuracy. Positive-control performance, low held-out shuffled-label accuracy, finite varying features, exact last-layer logit reconstruction, and unchanged frozen artifacts provide evidence that extraction and decoder training operated. Batched/single-example agreement missed its tolerance at four later layers, but passed at the selected layer, and authorization decisions agreed on all eight checked examples. This diagnostic failure does not establish an impossible result or a measurement bug.', 'validity': "This run measured sc1's own target: a frozen linear requested-file decoder applied to Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct's original final-prompt-token residual states on all 1,200 held-out four-file/four-recipient problems, balanced 600 permitted and 600 forbidden. Reported audits establish disjoint development/test names and permission mappings; training included 3,691 correct and 405 incorrect authorization runs. The catalog-position identity mapping, synthetic generator, A/B readout, and development-selected residual layer implement choices the claim leaves open, rather than substitute targets. The observed count exceeds sc1's 1,080-correct threshold under this protocol. The design-added numerical-agreement check failed at blocks 25–28 and remains a diagnostic limitation, although selected block 20 passed. Recipient decoding and attention-head patching were not evaluated, so this run cannot establish those separate requirements or the full conjunctive claim. Error-conditioned requested-file decoding was reported descriptively, not as another primary endpoint."}
