experiment_sc4 {'measures_claim_target': True, 'sound': True, 'via': 'llm', 'status': 'judged', 'answered_by': {'attempt': 1, 'model': 'openai/gpt-6.1-sol'}, 'reason': "The result is statistically plausible and internally consistent. Recipient decoding succeeds on 197/290 initial errors (67.93%; 95% Wilson interval 62.35–73.04%), below the required 261/290. Authorization-class error counts sum to 290, their decoder successes sum to 197, and initially correct plus incorrect decoder successes equal the full-test total: 654 + 197 = 851. Confusion matrices and paired-control differences also reconcile. The converged decoder performs substantially above the shuffled-label control, so this is a learned but imperfect readout, not evidence that training never operated. Missing 90% is a genuine negative result. The summary's full_test_criterion_met flag should not be interpreted as passing the overall decoding-accuracy threshold; the explicit full-test accuracy is only 70.92%.", 'validity': "This directly measures sc4: a development-frozen linear permitted-recipient decoder applied to Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct's original final prompt-token residual states on every initial authorization error in the balanced 1,200-problem held-out test. Reported checks confirm four files/four recipients, unseen names and structural assignments, and training on both correct and incorrect development runs. Directory-position labels, constrained Yes/No decisions, prompt distractions, and development-selected layer are admissible method choices, not substitutions. Qualification and learning checks passed. The published Base-model/eight-choice comparator is explicitly contextual, not a reproduction baseline. This implementation fails sc4's threshold, but does not exclude other admissible implementations of the existential claim. Requested-file decoding and head patching were not tested."}
