experiment_sc5 {'measures_claim_target': True, 'sound': True, 'via': 'llm', 'status': 'judged', 'answered_by': {'attempt': 1, 'model': 'openai/gpt-6.1-sol'}, 'reason': 'The completed result is statistically plausible and internally consistent. The 123 initial errors and 1,077 initially correct decisions sum to 1,200. Repairs are 112/123 = 91.06%, below the ceiling imposed by 121 errors with qualifying donors; disruption is 2/1,077 = 0.186%. The net gain is 112 − 2 = 110 decisions, giving (1,077 + 110)/1,200 = 98.9167% patched accuracy, exactly as reported. Confusion counts, Wilson intervals, bootstrap intervals, paired-test counts, and Holm adjustments agree with these totals. The intervention demonstrably operated: 1,198 cases received nonidentical activation replacements, downstream margins changed, and all 16 all-head reconstruction checks passed. Self-patching changed no decisions, while the random-head control produced a distinct, weaker result. The earlier donor-capture assertion failure belongs to an aborted attempt; the completed run reports zero capture-requalification failures and successful mechanism checks. No reported outcome establishes a statistical impossibility or a broken effect measurement.', 'validity': 'This directly measured sc5 on the named Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct checkpoint, using all 1,200 held-out four-file/four-recipient authorization problems, balanced 600/600. Reported novelty checks establish disjoint development/test names and canonical permission assignments. One development-fixed set of 11 query heads was patched from verified-correct donors differing only in permission-table row order, with the selection rule and semantic-token scope frozen before testing. Every initial error remained in the correction denominator, including two donor-unavailable no-op cases. The same intervention additionally measured correct-decision preservation. The synthetic generator, forced-choice readout, patch scope, and oracle donor verification instantiate choices the claim leaves open; they are not stand-ins. The adjacent GSM8K literature result is not an authorization-task baseline that this run was required to reproduce. The run measures the target repair rate for this particular setup, but does not test the decoder subclaims, establish the entire six-condition claim, or demonstrate production file-transfer safety.'}
