experiment_sc6 {'measures_claim_target': True, 'sound': True, 'via': 'llm', 'status': 'judged', 'answered_by': {'attempt': 1, 'model': 'openai/gpt-6.1-sol'}, 'validity': "This directly measured sc6's target: authorization-decision changes among all initially correct cases of the named Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct checkpoint on 1,200 balanced held-out four-file/four-recipient problems. The result reports unseen test names and disjoint permission assignments, development-frozen heads and donor rules, correct same-facts reordered donors, and identical intervention application to both initial outcome subsets. The mechanism demonstrably operated, with 213 repairs and nonzero effective replacements, so preservation was not measured using an inactive intervention. The observed disruption satisfies the scoped empirical threshold, and the same pipeline also satisfies its coupled repair qualification. Diagnostic limitation: strict custom-forward logit agreement failed on the two-example comparison, although decisions agreed and self-patch checks passed. The unrelated published steering comparator is explicitly not a reproduction baseline. No decoder accuracies or full six-part conjunction were tested. The run also does not establish generalization beyond the sampled setup or practical donor selection without access to authorization ground truth.", 'reason': 'SOUND. The primary counts and statistics are internally consistent: 971 initially correct cases plus 229 errors equal 1,200; repairing 213 errors while changing zero correct decisions yields 1,184/1,200 = 98.67% patched accuracy, versus 80.92% initially. Repair is 213/229 = 93.01%, and disruption is 0/971 = 0%. The label-specific accuracies reconcile with these totals. The reported Wilson intervals, one-sided Clopper–Pearson upper bound of 0.308%, and exact binomial p-value are consistent with their counts. Qualifying donors covered 219 errors and 970 correct cases; repairs do not exceed donor availability, and missing donors remain in the denominators. Nine heads across 1,189 accepted donors account for 10,701 replacements. Nonzero activation differences, substantial demonstrated repairs, exact self-patch reproduction, and only two repairs under the random-head control support actual intervention operation. High repair with zero observed disruption is not statistically impossible for this method. The custom-versus-standard forward comparison failed strict logit tolerance, but its 0.125 maximum difference is plausibly attributable to BF16 rounding, and sampled decisions agreed; this does not establish a contradictory result.'}
